(g)
maintain a register in such form as may be prescribed, showing the name of the Horticulture plant sold to any person, its
age, the name of the root stock and scion, bud wood and the name and the address of the person purchasing it, and
shall produce the record for inspection on demand by the Director or Inspecting officer;
(h)
exhibit the rates charged by him for each of the nursery plants sold by him at a conspicuous place in the nursery;
(i)
maintain a Bill Book and issue sale bill containing Book number, machine numbered bill, showing species, variety name,
quantity and sale rate in the nursery or by the trader;
(j)
the nursery register shall be preserved by the nurseryman for at least five years after the date of conclusion of the
transaction;
(k)
undertake to release for sale or distribution only such Horticulture plants as are completely free from any kind of pests or
disease;
(l)
keep the plants as well as the progeny trees used for the production of nursery plants free from any kind of pests and
disease;
(m)
